87
00:10:34,139 --> 00:10:40,139
Not only a little less than 1% as we are now using in the case of uranium.

88
00:10:45,999 --> 00:10:49,579
There are lots of reactors that could use thorium now.

89
00:10:53,359 --> 00:11:01,419
What is done is that the thorium is irradiated, it then transforms itself

90
00:11:02,479 --> 00:11:12,779
into a very valuable fuel uranium-233. You run the reactors on this fuel and make more uranium.

91
00:11:12,879 --> 00:11:21,000
The trouble is that in the reactors which are now available can do the Canadian heavy water reactor

92
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:31,220
or the high temperature gas cooled reactor or maybe a slight modification of the light water reactor,

93
00:11:31,779 --> 00:11:32,899
